# Local Engineering — Detailed Reference

On-demand elaboration for `local-engineering.prompt`. Read when your task
touches the PWA-vs-holistic-UI boundary or epic icon rendering — not on every
boot.

## Two phone-viewable surfaces, one boundary — Full Text
5. Two phone-viewable surfaces, one boundary — pick correctly at spec time.
   There are TWO web surfaces a developer can view on a phone, and they are NOT
   interchangeable: (a) the STATIC backlog-dashboard PWA (`pwa/index.html` ->
   `pwa/app.js`), a pure renderer that fetches `./backlog.json` — a
   git-SHA-reproducible PROJECTION with NO bridge/host connectivity, NO auth,
   and NO write path; and (b) the LIVE holistic UI
   (`extension/src/bridge/holisticUiHtml.ts`), served by `bridge/bridgeServer.ts`
   with token auth, which fetches live endpoints and can perform control actions.
   Only data derivable from git state at a SHA may ride `backlog.json`/the static
   PWA. Route any view that needs machine-local/live data, a host-persisted
   marker, or a control/write action to the LIVE holistic UI (and/or the
   host-side daily briefing) — never the static PWA; do not push machine-local
   data into the git projection. Confirm which surface a request means before
   speccing; "put it on the phone app" does not automatically mean the static
   PWA. (Recurred 3x in 2026-07-10: BL-252 suite-duration trend, BL-265
   gate-answer view, BL-257 slices 3-4 changed-since-visit + live trends.)

## Epics have icons representing musical forms — Full Text
6. Epics have icons representing musical forms. An epic is a large-scale
   musical FORM, so its icon is drawn from that vocabulary, on TWO distinct
   surfaces with two distinct realisations — never one implementation
   assumed to cover both: the PWA/fleet-console/bot-avatar surfaces carry the
   owned orchestra FORM marks (Symphony/Concerto/Suite/Fugue/Overture —
   `docs/branding/icon-system.md` §4d); Telegram topic icons stand in with
   the closest stock PERFORMANCE sticker instead, because the platform wall
   is real — `getForumTopicIconStickers` offers no notation/instrument
   glyphs, so an SVG form mark can never be pushed onto a Telegram topic
   icon, only approximated by a performance emoji (BL-449).

## Architecture Rules 2-6 and Diagrams/Key Integration — pre-second-trim wording (BL-858 further split)

`local-engineering.prompt`'s own text, verbatim, before BL-858's second pass:

2. Swarm machinery relationship. The swarm machinery under `swarmforge/` in this
   repo is a **maintained fork** of unclebob/swarm-forge, not an unmodified
   dependency. Local modifications are deliberate and tracked; upstream changes
   enter only through the drift-watch review (`upstream-watch.json`,
   `docs/upstream-deviations.md`), never by automatic fetch. The bootstrap
   wrapper must fetch helper scripts from a pinned by-SHA tarball, not a
   floating branch head.
5. Two phone-viewable surfaces, one boundary — pick correctly at spec time.
   TWO web surfaces are phone-viewable and are NOT interchangeable: (a) the
   STATIC backlog-dashboard PWA (`pwa/index.html` -> `pwa/app.js`), a pure
   renderer fetching `./backlog.json` — a git-SHA-reproducible PROJECTION
   with NO bridge/host connectivity, NO auth, NO write path; and (b) the LIVE
   holistic UI (`extension/src/bridge/holisticUiHtml.ts`, served by
   `bridge/bridgeServer.ts`) with token auth, live endpoints, and control
   actions. Only git-SHA-derivable data may ride the static PWA; route any
   live/machine-local/write-path need to the LIVE holistic UI instead —
   confirm which surface a request means before speccing. (Recurred 3x in
   2026-07-10: BL-252 suite-duration trend, BL-265 gate-answer view, BL-257
   slices 3-4 changed-since-visit + live trends.) See
   **local-engineering-detailed.prompt** for the fuller narrative.
6. Epics have icons representing musical forms, on TWO distinct surfaces
   with two distinct realisations — never one implementation assumed to
   cover both: the PWA/fleet-console/bot-avatar surfaces carry the owned
   orchestra FORM marks (Symphony/Concerto/Suite/Fugue/Overture —
   `docs/branding/icon-system.md` §4d); Telegram topic icons stand in with
   the closest stock PERFORMANCE sticker instead, since
   `getForumTopicIconStickers` offers no notation/instrument glyphs. See
   **local-engineering-detailed.prompt** for the BL-449 platform-wall
   rationale.

### Diagrams (this project) — pre-second-trim wording

Per the shared Diagrams rule, the diagrams this project maintains are:
1. **Architecture diagram** — the two-layer system: extension host,
   webview(s), the tmux substrate, `.swarmforge/` state, handoffd and the
   queue helpers, and the boundaries between them (what talks to what, and
   over which channel: postMessage, files, tmux socket, git).
2. **Swarm workflow flow diagram** — the CURRENT parcel flow: intake at the
   backlog root, specifier speccing to paused/, coordinator promotion and
   assignment, the specifier→coder→cleaner→architect→hardender→documenter→QA
   chain, QA approval, merge-up broadcast to worktree roles, and coordinator
   integration on `main` (close ticket, promote next). When the pipeline
   topology or backlog flow changes, this diagram changes in the same
   parcel.
Both live under `docs/diagrams/` as Mermaid sources.

## Architecture Rule 1, Testability Boundary, Key Integration Surface — pre-third-trim wording (BL-858 further split)

`local-engineering.prompt`'s own text, verbatim, before BL-858's third pass:

1. Two layers: tile-as-view, tmux-as-substrate. Tiles are TypeScript/webview
   VIEWS; tmux is the process SUBSTRATE running the agents. These are layers,
   not alternatives. Do NOT spawn agent processes directly from TypeScript to
   bypass tmux — if a task starts to feel like rebuilding process orchestration,
   stop: that is the signal the line was crossed.

## Testability Boundary — Bubble (Android) (BL-769)
Per the shared Design And Testability rule, this project's environmentally
unsuitable boundary also includes the **Android device surface**: Activities/
Services, the overlay window, audio capture/playback, and real network I/O
against a live tunnel. **Pure logic** (no `android.*` type in the function's
signature) is covered by the plain-JUnit JVM suite (`./gradlew
:app:testDebugUnitTest`, no emulator) — push framework types to the thin
device edge. **Device-surface behavior** is verified by a recorded manual
procedure noted in the ticket; never ship a Bubble feature file whose
scenarios have no runnable binding. Robolectric/`androidTest` deliberately
not adopted.

## Key Integration Surface
Prove these against a real swarm install, in order, before UI polish:
1. Launch a swarm against a target path by shelling to ./swarm.
2. Discover the tmux socket (.swarmforge/tmux-socket) and enumerate
   sessions/windows/panes.
3. Tail one pane's output into a webview tile, live.
4. Send keystrokes INTO a pane (fiddliest cross-platform piece — tackle early).
5. Read .swarmforge/ state to know which stage holds the work.
6. Open a PR from the dev branch into the target's main via git + GitHub CLI/API.

If any of these cannot be done from outside the swarm machinery, note it clearly
as a candidate change to the fork (via the normal backlog), rather than working
around it ad hoc.

## Interface vs incarnation — Full Text (BL-858)
7. Interface vs incarnation — two naming layers, deliberately. Architecture
   and forward-looking prose may name the INTERFACES: **messaging** (the
   human chat channel / chat adapter) and **host agent** (the IDE seat that
   drives Remote verbs, pairing, and pack staffing). Everyday operator speech
   names the live INCARNATIONS: **Telegram** (messaging) and **Cursor** (host
   agent). The phone app's product name is **Bubble** (native Android under
   `android/`; BL-707) — do not introduce a parallel brand (Float Companion,
   companion app, overlay app) in new prose, though historical ticket titles
   and the `floatcompanion` package id may stay. Doc style: "the host agent
   (today: Cursor) …", "messaging (today: Telegram) …", "the phone app is
   **Bubble** …". A proposal to rename identifiers, env vars, files, or
   how-tos to erase Telegram/Cursor "for purity" is OUT OF POLICY: the
   specifier does not spec it and the coordinator does not promote it, unless
   the human explicitly asks for a second messaging app or a second
   host-agent backend AND a shim plan. Dual-name shims belong at adapter
   edges when a real second incarnation lands — never as a vocabulary chore.
   (Human directive 2026-07-30, `backlog/INTAKE-messaging-host-agent-interface-vs-incarnation.md`.)

## Testability Boundary — Bubble (Android) (BL-769) — Full Text (BL-858)
Per the shared Design And Testability rule, this project's environmentally
unsuitable boundary includes — alongside the VS Code Extension API surface,
the webview execution context, and live tmux/PTY interaction — the **Android
device surface**: Activities and Services as running components, the overlay
window, audio capture and playback, and real network I/O against a live
tunnel.

Every Bubble behavior lands on one side of a stated line — none is left with
neither:
- **Pure logic** (no `android.*` framework type in the function's own
  signature: parsing, classification, data transforms) is covered by the
  plain-JUnit JVM unit suite under `android/app/src/test/`, run via
  `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest` with no emulator and no connected
  device. Push framework types to the thin device edge (e.g. the Activity
  converts `android.net.Uri` to `String` before calling the parser) — the
  same thin-edge rule this article already applies to the VS Code API and
  the webview. Robolectric and emulator-backed `androidTest` are
  deliberately not adopted; introducing either is its own ticket, never a
  drive-by test dependency.
- **Device-surface behavior** is verified by a recorded manual procedure
  noted in the ticket. The Node acceptance runner cannot execute Kotlin:
  never ship a Bubble feature file whose scenarios have no runnable binding —
  bind them to step handlers that drive the gradle unit suite (as
  BL-769's do), or record the manual procedure the ticket will be verified
  by.

How-to: `docs/how-to/BL-769-android-jvm-unit-suite.md`.

## npm runs from `extension/`, never the repo root — pre-BL-883 boot wording (BL-883 split)

- **npm runs from `extension/`, never the repo root.** The root has no
  `package.json`; the tracked `package-lock.json` sitting there is a stray,
  unreferenced artifact (BL-875 removes it). Until it is gone, `npm install`
  from the root fails ENOENT — but rewrites that lockfile's `"name"` to the
  cwd basename FIRST, leaving an unexplained one-line root diff that rides
  along in your commit and breaches "An Approval Authorizes Only Its Ticket's
  Work" (BL-506). Verified 2026-08-10: `npm install` rewrites it, `npm run`
  and `npm ci` do not. Recover with `git restore -- package-lock.json`, never
  `git stash` (stash is repo-wide across every worktree). Reported by the
  hardener from a live GH-26 near-miss.
